{#
  BeMart Login page — EC-CUBE goLogin.

  PORT of EC-CUBE 4.3 default-theme `Mypage/login.twig`
  (src/Eccube/Resource/template/default/Mypage/login.twig).

  Markup skeleton, `ec-role` / `ec-pageHeader` / `ec-off2Grid` /
  `ec-login` / `ec-grid2` classes and structure are kept verbatim from
  EC-CUBE. Only the dynamic bindings are rebound to the Login resource
  body (src/Resource/Page/Login.php).

  Phase 3 — FORM page (Ray.WebFormModule pilot). The login inputs are
  now rendered through a real form object — `LoginForm` (an
  AbstractForm), exposed by the Login resource as `body.form`:

    {{ form.input('email') }}   <- real <input> w/ id/attrs/value
    {{ form.error('email') }}   <- inline Be-domain error, if any

  EC-CUBE renders the same inputs through the Symfony FormView
  (`form_widget(form.email)`); Ray.WebFormModule (Aura.Input +
  Aura.Html) is BeMart's BEAR-idiomatic equivalent. The field names /
  ids / attributes in LoginForm::init() are ported from EC-CUBE's
  `CustomerLoginType` + the template's `form_widget` `attr` options, so
  the rendered markup carries EC-CUBE's `ec-*` form shape.

  Validation authority stays with the Be Framework Becoming chain — the
  form is a field-definition + renderer. On a domain rejection the Login
  resource repopulates `form` (entered email) and the resource body
  carries the form-level `message`, rendered below in the EC-CUBE
  `ec-errorMessage` <p> exactly as EC-CUBE's `error` block does.

  EC-CUBE-ism rebinding (see var/templates/README.md):
   - `{{ 'key'|trans }}`  -> the ja literal from messages.ja.yaml.
   - `csrf_token('authenticate')` — EC-CUBE per-request CSRF widget.
     BeMart keeps the hidden `_csrf_token` input and fills it from the
     dev/html fake CSRF token so a browser submit reaches the login POST
     path. EC-CUBE-runtime token generation remains a residual.
   - `app.session.flashBag.*`, `is_granted(...)`, `BaseInfo.*`
     — request-flash / auth-state / BaseInfo runtime. The remember-me
     checkbox depends on `BaseInfo.option_remember_me`; BeMart has no
     BaseInfo, so it is OMITTED (never invented) and noted as residual.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% set body_class = 'mypage' %}
{% set route = 'login' %}
{% set title = 'ログイン' %}

{% block main %}
    <div class="ec-role">
        <div class="ec-pageHeader">
            <h1>ログイン</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="ec-off2Grid">
            <div class="ec-off2Grid__cell">
                <form class="doLogin" name="login_mypage" id="login_mypage" method="post" action="/login">
                    <div class="ec-login">
                        <div class="ec-login__icon">
                            <div class="ec-icon"><img src="{{ asset('assets/icon/user.svg') }}" alt=""></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="ec-login__input">
                            <div class="ec-input">
                                {{ form.input('email')|raw }}
                                {{ form.error('email') }}
                                {{ form.input('password')|raw }}
                                {{ form.error('password') }}
                            </div>
                            {% if message is defined and message %}
                                <p class="ec-errorMessage">{{ message }}</p>
                            {% endif %}
                        </div>
                        <div class="ec-grid2">
                            <div class="ec-grid2__cell">
                                <div class="ec-login__actions">
                                    <button type="submit"
                                            class="ec-blockBtn--cancel">ログイン</button>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="ec-grid2__cell">
                                <div class="ec-login__link"><a class="ec-link goForgotPassword"
                                                               href="/forgot-password">ログイン情報をお忘れですか？</a>
                                </div>
                                <div class="ec-login__link"><a class="ec-link"
                                                               href="/entry">新規会員登録</a>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <input type="hidden" name="mode" value="login">
                    <input type="hidden" name="csrfToken" value="{{ csrfToken|default(csrf_token()) }}">
                </form>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
